        'Real telemetry from a robot — bus voltage and current, per-joint temperature and current, IMU vibration RMS, perception frame rate and confidence, comms RSSI/latency/loss, storage free space and write errors, safety chain status, CPU/GPU load and temperature, calibration age and residuals, network topology, payload state, and log integrity — is streamed to a dashboard. Anomaly detection runs on that telemetry: per-channel z-scores and EWMA control limits, a Mahalanobis distance on the correlation structure, and optionally a small autoencoder on windows. Alerts fire on statistical evidence, and every alert carries the channel and the threshold that triggered it.',
