      'PV arrays produce dangerous DC voltage whenever lit: cover panels before wiring, use insulated tools, and never work on a live array in wet conditions. DC arcs do not self-extinguish — use DC-rated breakers and fuses.',
      'Battery bank energy is lethal: a 48 V 200 Ah bank stores ~9.6 kWh. Insulate all tools, remove jewellery, work one hand at a time, and install a Class T or equivalent DC fuse at the battery terminal.',
